m/users/clarkbw/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clarkbw/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clarkbw/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clarkbw","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sailingnaturali/claude-skills/commits/7d589dd5e4ddb554117f7540ab7cb80269996e9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:59:23Z","email":"clarkbw@gmail.com","name":"Bryan Clark"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T12:59:58Z","email":"clarkbw@gmail.com","name":"Bryan Clark"},"message":"signalk-e2e: fold the two e2e skills into one plugin, address review\n\nReview on #2 requested: one plugin with two co-installed skills instead of\ntwo separate plugins (so signalk-server-e2e can safely reference webapp-e2e).\n\n- Restructure signalk-server-e2e + webapp-e2e into a single signalk-e2e plugin\n  (signalk-e2e/skills/{signalk-server-e2e,webapp-e2e}/); one plugin.json, one\n  marketplace entry, one README section.\n- Slim signalk-server-e2e to the SignalK-specific layer (server spin-up, WS\n  deltas, Freeboard recipe) and defer shared mechanics to webapp-e2e.\n- Version-stamp the Freeboard-SK recipe (v2.x, July 2026) with a re-verify note.\n- Make the fetch-poll the primary readiness gate, networkidle the fallback\n  (a SignalK UI holds its delta WebSocket open, so idle may never fire).\n- Add server teardown (kill the process, rm -rf the scratch config dir).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DAdcmd4JxY8bUzKVrJH7NT","tree":{"sha":"e2ff4d7983bc0bba15ead1b95411197ac01d3dc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sailingnaturali/claude-skills/git/trees/e2ff4d7983bc0bba15ead1b95411197ac01d3dc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sailingnaturali/claude-skills/git/commits/7d589dd5e4ddb554117f7540ab7cb80269996e9c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"u