m/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commit/957dcd68ddffa7ea827741d7fcd32a64227ccf4c","node_id":"C_kwDOSypr6NoAKDk1N2RjZDY4ZGRmZmE3ZWE4Mjc3NDFkN2ZjZDMyYTY0MjI3Y2NmNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commit/48896b179f4c5f3d605edd0c49f697f60a510fde","sha":"48896b179f4c5f3d605edd0c49f697f60a510fde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commits/48896b179f4c5f3d605edd0c49f697f60a510fde"}],"sha":"957dcd68ddffa7ea827741d7fcd32a64227ccf4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commits/957dcd68ddffa7ea827741d7fcd32a64227ccf4c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3533280?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brightq","id":3533280,"login":"brightq","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MzMyODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commits/48896b179f4c5f3d605edd0c49f697f60a510fde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T14:28:50Z","email":"brightq@gmail.com","name":"BrightQi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T14:28:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(320): live model catalog via BFF listModels + SDK 0.18.0 (π2 studio) (#14)\n\n* feat(#320): live model catalog via BFF listModels + SDK 0.18.0\n\nReplace the static MODEL_CATALOG with a live backend catalog fetched\nfrom a new BFF `GET /models` action that calls `client.catalog.list()`\n(ADMIN_SECRET-gated). The static list is kept as an offline/dev fallback,\nclearly marked. Bumps contract 0.3.0→0.4.0, bff 0.4.0→0.5.0,\nweb 0.3.0→0.4.0; upgrades @baobox/sdk to ^0.18.0 in bff; normalizes\nSDK 0.18.0 null reasoningEffort to undefined at the BFF boundary.\n\n- contract: add listModels route, LlmCatalog schemas/types, drift-guard\n  test for REASONING_EFFORT_VALUES (#320)\n- bff: add GET /models handler, normalizeSkillDetail for null→undefined,\n  add listModels to SkillStudioReadOp, 5 new authoring tests\n- web: add fetchModelCatalog(), liveToLocal projection, async catalog load\n  in EditableSkill with MODEL_CATALOG fallback, api.ts listModels method\n- docs: update SKILL_STUDIO_INTEGRATION.md version table + GET /models\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(320): bump contract @baobox/sdk dep to ^0.18.0 (reasoningEffort on SkillWithFiles)\n\nThe contract re-exports SkillWithFiles from @baobox/sdk; its dep was pinned\n^0.13.0 (pre-reasoningEffort). CI''s clean install gave the contract a nested\n0.13.x SDK lacking reasoningEffort, so the BFF (importing SkillWithFiles via\nthe contract) failed tsc (TS2339). Local dedupe to 0.18.0 had masked it.\nAlign with the BFF''s ^0.18.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac0ae9ddbf5cc3d2a79fc4dff76afa2e1710a7fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/git/trees/ac0ae9ddbf5cc3d2a79fc4dff76afa2e1710a7fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/git/commits/48896b179f4c5f3d605edd0c49f697f60a510fde","verification":{"payload":"tree ac0ae9ddbf5cc3d2a79fc4dff76afa2e1710a7fe\nparent 5ac399c9a95246691c079b94a81028b0c329f121\nauthor BrightQi <brightq@gmail.com> 1781879330 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781879330 +0800\n\nfeat(320): live model catalog via BFF listModels + SDK 0.18.0 (π2 studio) (#14)\n\n* feat(#320): live model catalog via BFF listModels + SDK 0.18.0\n\nReplace the static MODEL_CATALOG with a live backend catalog fetched\nfrom a new BFF `GET /models` action that calls `client.catalog.list()`\n(ADMIN_SECRET-gated). The static list is kept as an offline/dev fallback,\nclearly marked. Bumps contract 0.3.0→0.4.0, bff 0.4.0→0.5.0,\nweb 0.3.0→0.4.0; upgrades @baobox/sdk to ^0.18.0 in bff; normalizes\nSDK 0.18.0 null reasoningEffort to undefined at the BFF boundary.\n\n- contract: add listModels route, LlmCatalog schemas/types, drift-guard\n  test for REASONING_EFFORT_VALUES (#320)\n- bff: add GET /models handler, normalizeSkillDetail for null→undefined,\n  add listModels to SkillStudioReadOp, 5 new authoring tests\n- web: add fetchModelCatalog(), liveToLocal projection, async catalog load\n  in EditableSkill with MODEL_CATALOG fallback, api.ts listModels method\n- docs: update SKILL_STUDIO_INTEGRATION.md version table + GET /models\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(320): bump contract @baobox/sdk dep to ^0.18.0 (reasoningEffort on SkillWithFiles)\n\nThe contract re-exports SkillWithFiles from @baobox/sdk; its dep was pinned\n^0.13.0 (pre-reasoningEffort). CI''s clean install gave the contract a nested\n0.13.x SDK lacking reasoningEffort, so the BFF (importing SkillWithFiles via\nthe contract) failed tsc (TS2339). Local dedupe to 0.18.0 had masked it.\nAlign with the BFF''s ^0.18.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNVIiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALbwQAItIrC6Ab+juYCI1xovafEgS\n2G83heWaX7JXnOPAZk3ahuqlpbXm5pYcT40JrPzvtyHwoltHKrLajMqHcPN9eWCV\nIc4sOUj34fc6BKPXuw/56QqVTRHy618HeafnOa8bV4ZA4hUUmM2JqNUui3Rxk2V/\nEItC0w46Yin/izhOV7RB1PwW7fLqoLv3UrYZ36kJ0jGsnLx6ew5pr/cgk7p4BAR/\nJo3kUMyMfL6uTjI45OH2t8EFHOs5zkcXqacon7CvXcKl7wBLA1GQRWj0aVNZ6R5p\nYbcvDwSc6FI/UepdKCoYpeyfpO7GVjt8qTWUWEZs55OmO7zEvYsN5rIMJV50sza7\n1IHBOrVrHUfGAVj0j8mkOoWHGA5Z6sUS19WVy8LWd6QGoTABJU2rtH3VqCL5etT4\nZMrZPz1FNC4V4oyxKmQLdLInYXHxMg3hgQtxsNo1C58GJBsChEr5YrjozbsE9sDb\n3zHJv9Ag8rP+SYmtojskmzCbfSs6mQvkIOFPltVyDi4aoA1m8i9zqUH9hk3XMFlU\ncTprC9L7XFwVbb7o8xB72iCX4HAibjsw9ZQs5kjxHeZBnoQGtQvidzXQKWNLYBy6\nAgZiYcdu1yb8S4u21mD85IC8HqPGzpriJRFgX18aO2cUh/rrKHEcCCFA/1xNZgUO\nwsPXFsyhujxA7frnvbRT\n=FLn/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-19T14:28:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commit/48896b179f4c5f3d605edd0c49f697f60a510fde","node_id":"C_kwDOSypr6NoAKDQ4ODk2YjE3OWY0YzVmM2Q2MDVlZGQwYzQ5ZjY5N2Y2MGE1MTBmZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commit/5ac399c9a95246691c079b94a81028b0c329f121","sha":"5ac399c9a95246691c079b94a81028b0c329f121","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commits/5ac399c9a95246691c079b94a81028b0c329f121"}],"sha":"48896b179f4c5f3d605edd0c49f697f60a510fde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commits/48896b179f4c5f3d605edd0c49f697f60a510fde"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3533280?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brightq","id":3533280,"login":"brightq","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MzMyODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commits/5ac399c9a95246691c079b94a81028b0c329f121/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T04:36:10Z","email":"brightq@gmail.com","name":"BrightQi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T04:36:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(312): Skill Studio tool picker via listAvailableTools allowlist (π5) (#13)\n\nPart of Epic π #310. Replaces the attach-by-id-only tool input in Skill\nStudio with a real picker, by adding an allowlist-enumeration action to the\nBFF surface. No BaoBox backend or SDK change — the SDK already exposes\n`client.tools.list()` (apiKey-gated, own + global = the attachable set).\n\n- contract: new `listAvailableTools` route (GET /tools) + ListAvailableTools\n  response type, distinct from the attached-tools route (GET /skills/:id/tools).\n- bff: new GET /tools handler — authz(\"listAvailableTools\") → client.tools.list()\n  → projects to a lean { id, name, description } summary. SECURITY: drops\n  handlerConfig / inputSchema so callback secrets never reach the browser\n  (this is a public-repo MFE); credentials stay in runtime config only.\n- web: api.listAvailableTools(); ToolsPanel now offers a picker sourced from\n  it (excluding already-attached tools), with the free-text attach-by-id kept\n  as a fallback if the list call fails — the server stays the allowlist\n  authority (tool_not_allowed handling preserved).\n- docs: SKILL_STUDIO_INTEGRATION.md lists the new action.\n- versions: contract 0.3.0, bff 0.4.0, web 0.3.0 (publish is a separate gated\n  step — not tagged/published here).\n\nGates: typecheck (3/3), build (3/3), tests contract 38 / bff 61 / web 43,\npublish --dry-run clean for all three. No secrets/hostnames added.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"764205bef0092d0e27d049ee9df84840dad6da9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/git/trees/764205bef0092d0e27d049ee9df84840dad6da9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/git/commits/5ac399c9a95246691c079b94a81028b0c329f121","verification":{"payload":"tree 764205bef0092d0e27d049ee9df84840dad6da9a\nparent cc349855cbf78e520d983dff5cd1bd52f117eb0d\nauthor BrightQi <brightq@gmail.com> 1781843770 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781843770 +0800\n\nfeat(312): Skill Studio tool picker via listAvailableTools allowlist (π5) (#13)\n\nPart of Epic π #310. Replaces the attach-by-id-only tool input in Skill\nStudio with a real picker, by adding an allowlist-enumeration action to the\nBFF surface. No BaoBox backend or SDK change — the SDK already exposes\n`client.tools.list()` (apiKey-gated, own + global = the attachable set).\n\n- contract: new `listAvailableTools` route (GET /tools) + ListAvailableTools\n  response type, distinct from the attached-tools route (GET /skills/:id/tools).\n- bff: new GET /tools handler — authz(\"listAvailableTools\") → client.tools.list()\n  → projects to a lean { id, name, description } summary. SECURITY: drops\n  handlerConfig / inputSchema so callback secrets never reach the browser\n  (this is a public-repo MFE); credentials stay in runtime config only.\n- web: api.listAvailableTools(); ToolsPanel now offers a picker sourced from\n  it (excluding already-attached tools), with the free-text attach-by-id kept\n  as a fallback if the list call fails — the server stays the allowlist\n  authority (tool_not_allowed handling preserved).\n- docs: SKILL_STUDIO_INTEGRATION.md lists the new action.\n- versions: contract 0.3.0, bff 0.4.0, web 0.3.0 (publish is a separate gated\n  step — not tagged/published here).\n\nGates: typecheck (3/3), build (3/3), tests contract 38 / bff 61 / web 43,\npublish --dry-run clean for all three. No secrets/hostnames added.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNMc6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9q4QADMv3UtyTYpzvNOa4znUiNq2\nJt2tfi/wHHTzV/1iH0jTbiJClGzHEwsACDSYRwyRwH6yZ0jPOvFOgs6zYremT4z2\nxAVo78+gGx7GXC5kBQ+4GwzkPSwlxxC/m04CyxODDtTHyycXtlCRa8zturKaddkO\njFaUerKSTHaJZaN2Hs8+dGqJ1N3B/N1xYgSpAGVsd16itjm9sg3Cwxd1LJi2IwMB\n1DYIaytlN6On1CR