the\n@baobox/sdk apiKey path (all tenant-scoped):\n\n- POST /skills (create, tenant-owned, 201) · PUT /skills/:id (structural update)\n- GET|POST /skills/:id/attached-skills + DELETE …/:childId (sub-skill graph;\n  worker 422 → contract cycle_detected)\n- GET|POST /skills/:id/tools + DELETE …/:toolId (tool wiring; worker 403 →\n  tool_not_allowed). listTools is PROJECTED to {id,name,description} — the SDK\n  Tool''s handlerConfig/inputSchema (possible callback secrets) never reach the\n  browser.\n- GET|PUT /skills/:id/parameters (per-tenant parameters)\n\nNew hooks:\n- onMutation({op,skillId,before?,after?,childSkillId?,toolId?}) — the git-truth\n  control point. Fires after a structural mutation commits so the host can record\n  drift / queue promote-back. Notification, not a gate (authz is the gate);\n  throwing onMutation never fails the request (audited). Default no-op.\n- parameters store ({get,set}) — per-tenant params have no BaoBox backing, so\n  persistence is host-delegated. No store → GET returns [], PUT refused (403).\n  secret:true values are masked (blanked) in every response.\n\nOther:\n- Extended the authz op union + AuditRecord to the new ops (childSkillId/toolId).\n- Normalized upstream errors to the contract''s stable ContractErrorCode enum with\n  op-aware disambiguation; Phase-1 validation code is now validation_error.\n- Bumped @baobox/sdk ^0.16.0, @baobox/skill-builder-contract ^0.2.0; root override\n  pins one sdk across the workspace.\n\nUnchanged: credential redaction, fail-closed authz, exactly-one-credential, and\nthe Phase-1 list/get/PATCH + sourceOfTruth read decorators.\n\n+25 tests (51 total, all green): create/structural/attach/detach/tools/params,\ncycle + allowlist mapping, tool-projection secret hygiene, parameter masking,\nfail-closed authz on every new op, best-effort onMutation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(259): redact credentials from validation-error messages + add review tests\n\nCodex review follow-up:\n- HIGH: validationError() now runs the Zod issue message through redact(), so a\n  strict-schema parse on a body that smuggled a credential-named key can''t echo\n  it on the wire (parity with respondError''s redaction on every other path).\n- Tests (+3): credential-redaction via a validation error, tenant-scope threading\n  on listAttachedSkills/listTools/getParameters, and onMutation failure isolation\n  across structural-update / attach-sub-skill / attach-tool.\n\n54 tests green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a4df702ed2e091d373aa44d7896ef81ff409a9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/git/trees/2a4df702ed2e091d373aa44d7896ef81ff409a9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/git/commits/023fb4576ce024396fd0a490135fd20d8ad4f85d","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a4df702ed2e091d373aa44d7896ef81ff409a9a\nparent 5fcb2e85a43db560d75d2b656b030cd1cf967c74\nauthor BrightQi <brightq@gmail.com> 1780820294 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780820294 +0800\n\nfeat(259): BFF Phase-2 authoring endpoints + git-truth onMutation hook — bff 0.3.0 (#8)\n\n* feat(259): BFF Phase-2 authoring endpoints + git-truth onMutation hook — bff 0.3.0\n\nImplements the @baobox/skill-builder-contract Phase-2 authoring surface over the\n@baobox/sdk apiKey path (all tenant-scoped):\n\n- POST /skills (create, tenant-owned, 201) · PUT /skills/:id (structural update)\n- GET|POST /skills/:id/attached-skills + DELETE …/:childId (sub-skill graph;\n  worker 422 → contract cycle_detected)\n- GET|POST /skills/:id/tools + DELETE …/:toolId (tool wiring; worker 403 →\n  tool_not_allowed). listTools is PROJECTED to {id,name,description} — the SDK\n  Tool''s handlerConfig/inputSchema (possible callback secrets) never reach the\n  browser.\n- GET|PUT /skills/:id/parameters (per-tenant parameters)\n\nNew hooks:\n- onMutation({op,skillId,before?,after?,childSkillId?,toolId?}) — the git-truth\n  control point. Fires after a structural mutation commits so the host can record\n  drift / queue promote-back. Notification, not a gate (authz is the gate);\n  throwing onMutation never fails the request (audited). Default no-op.\n- parameters store ({get,set}) — per-tenant params have no BaoBox backing, so\n  persistence is host-delegated. No store → GET returns [], PUT refused (403).\n  secret:true values are masked (blanked) in every response.\n\nOther:\n- Extended the authz op union + AuditRecord to the new ops (childSkillId/toolId).\n- Normalized upstream errors to the contract''s stable ContractErrorCode enum with\n  op-aware disambiguation; Phase-1 validation code is now validation_error.\n- Bumped @baobox/sdk ^0.16.0, @baobox/skill-builder-contract ^0.2.0; root override\n  pins one sdk across the workspace.\n\nUnchanged: credential redaction, fail-closed authz, exactly-one-credential, and\nthe Phase-1 list/get/PATCH + sourceOfTruth read decorators.\n\n+25 tests (51 total, all green): create/structural/attach/detach/tools/params,\ncycle + allowlist mapping, tool-projection secret hygiene, parameter masking,\nfail-closed authz on every new op, best-effort onMutation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(259): redact credentials from validation-error messages + add review tests\n\nCodex review follow-up:\n- HIGH: validationError() now runs the Zod issue message through redact(), so a\n  strict-schema parse on a body that smuggled a credential-named key can''t echo\n  it on the wire (parity with respondError''s redaction on every other path).\n- Tests (+3): credential-redaction via a validation error, tenant-scope threading\n  on listAttachedSkills/listTools/getParameters, and onMutation failure isolation\n  across structural-update / attach-sub-skill / attach-tool.\n\n54 tests green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJSlGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADVEQAIhC6iGzWVOeXfGf/WkSxfA1\nWuvRlfHcSetCvjvN4s/kSupHnsRVOG2k3ESGMvPs9AQEKohvR+9c7bCclkYbehXB\nhWQPn3kMW+ayBIkBMrA7lZzPIUNtjp++XdKtern7rXjaSo+F0wb/XcDjR2YUI96d\n6/xWZhguDMZ2Nqzgbqbc8MkgWMdj0SsoJAYX6v9TDC7xlQr7baGUc5Eec0fnh6p2\nWLzOpWc8dGnnJE3g6kPNXY1cbJQjHY32yDlg/sKI2c3YNlv+u9kb//QieoDlL+zs\nAE9bRNrfnHK2mwp089hE+YjCErQqK9CcQt69E+05fO1FmKyBZ/i+6jRJMgOykUt7\na/tqAniYpOSMs2NfLbnhJVVCHkaQQgbhpF65RBbv/MS2Emx6/FJ0v/c0UYgg+Sx0\nVdvvy00cCAO2va1PZu2rkp/mOGqJ9EUTOhCbVgY1M6qrtemtKLK6rMJgrmBa/3Um\nK9IWt5c1GyAG7v3nG0eBXIUR+GxXLpS43J01vWJvYhuLdyVotX6sALMOMQ+8wVIW\nzKFiJlBKSHAoB7p1HA91FW7cNNZSaEqQANGprYOKwDZefCinwWIJZyGrHqB1WMcB\nzxZf/0SxF+GbkFQURoMrdRIQCG6I9qQFu+nJvep0hkECErmRCOmC/jA/ENYkwJzh\nsvCM5OHtI+KoCnwvu1Ft\n=Pz/9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T08:18:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commit/023fb4576ce024396fd0a490135fd20d8ad4f85d","node_id":"C_kwDOSypr6NoAKDAyM2ZiNDU3NmNlMDI0Mzk2ZmQwYTQ5MDEzNWZkMjBkOGFkNGY4NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commit/5fcb2e85a43db560d75d2b656b030cd1cf967c74","sha":"5fcb2e85a43db560d75d2b656b030cd1cf967c74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commits/5fcb2e85a43db560d75d2b656b030cd1cf967c74"}],"sha":"023fb4576ce024396fd0a490135fd20d8ad4f85d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commits/023fb4576ce024396fd0a490135fd20d8ad4f85d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3533280?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brightq","id":3533280,"login":"brightq","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MzMyODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brightq","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/commits/5fcb2e85a43db560d75d2b656b030cd1cf967c74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T03:08:31Z","email":"brightq@gmail.com","name":"BrightQi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T03:08:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(258): extend contract for Phase-2 authoring — 0.2.0 (#7)\n\n* feat(258): extend contract for Phase-2 authoring — 0.2.0\n\nSkill Studio Phase 2 (#258). Grows the BFF↔MFE contract from the Phase-1 slice\n(list / get / single-field PATCH) to the full orchestrator authoring surface.\nFully ADDITIVE — every Phase-1 route + schema is unchanged.\n\nRoutes (skillStudioRoutes): createSkill (POST /skills), updateSkillStructural\n(PUT /skills/:id, multi-field), list/attach/detach sub-skills\n(/skills/:id/attached-skills[/:childId]), list/attach/detach tools\n(/skills/:id/tools[/:toolId]), get/set per-tenant parameters\n(/skills/:id/parameters).\n\nSchemas + types: skillCreateRequestSchema, skillStructuralUpdateRequestSchema\n(multi-field, >=1, strict), attachSubSkillRequestSchema, attachToolRequestSchema,\nskillParameterSchema / setSkillParametersRequestSchema, lean read projections\n(skillToolSummarySchema) + new response envelopes.\n\nContract error shape: contractErrorSchema + contractErrorCodeSchema\n(validation_error / cycle_detected / tool_not_allowed / forbidden / not_found /\nconflict / upstream_error / internal_error) so the Web Component branches on a\nstable code (clear cycle / allowlist / validation messages).\n\nCompile-time drift guards tie the create/structural editable fields to the SDK\nSkill type. 0.2.0 + CHANGELOG. +14 contract tests (31 total). All workspaces\ngreen (contract 31, bff 26, web 12). package-lock regenerated (also fixes the\npre-existing bff sdk 0.14->0.15 drift).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(258): keep Phase-1 route builders byte-for-byte unchanged (Codex)\n\nCodex review flagged that the Phase-1 getSkill/updateSkill builders had been\nmechanically rewritten to the new `enc` alias (runtime-identical to\nencodeURIComponent, but not byte-for-byte the Phase-1 source). Reverted both to\ninline encodeURIComponent; `enc` is used only by the new Phase-2 builders, so\nthe Phase-1 surface is now provably untouched. No behavior change.\n\n(Codex L1 — a reverse create→schema drift guard — is intentionally omitted: it\ncannot typecheck because Skill.sourceUrl is `string|null` while the create\nschema''s is `string|undefined`; the one-directional guard matches the existing\n_updateTracksSkill pattern.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"220a17d5d6cbcb54405af18a625caa5c775626ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/git/trees/220a17d5d6cbcb54405af18a625caa5c775626ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/baobox-ai/baobox-skill-studio/git/commits/5fcb2e85a43db560d75d2b656b030cd1cf967c74","verification":{"payload":"tree 220a17d5d6cbcb54405af18a625caa5c775626ac\nparent f94e8d4cda3e0dd49667d94af198dfef3b4c1092\nauthor BrightQi <brightq@gmail.com> 1780801711 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780801711 +0800\n\nfeat(258): extend contract for Phase-2 authoring — 0.2.0 (#7)\n\n* feat(258): extend contract for Phase-2 authoring — 0.2.0\n\nSkill Studio Phase 2 (#258). Grows the BFF↔MFE contract from the Phase-1 slice\n(list / get / single-field PATCH) to the full orchestrator authoring surface.\nFully ADDITIVE — every Phase-1 route + schema is unchanged.\n\nRoutes (skillStudioRoutes): createSkill (POST /skills), updateSkillStructural\n(PUT /skills/:id, multi-field), list/attach/detach sub-skills\n(/skills/:id/attached-skills[/:childId]), list/attach/detach tools\n(/skills/:id/tools[/:toolId]), get/set per-tenant parameters\n(/skills/:id/parameters).\n\nSchemas + types: skillCreateRequestSchema, skillStructuralUpdateRequestSchema\n(multi-field, >=1, strict), attachSubSkillRequestSchema, attachToolRequestSchema,\nskillParameterSchema / setSkillParametersRequestSchema, lean read projections\n(skillToolSummarySchema) + new response envelopes.\n\nContract error shape: contractErrorSchema + contractErrorCodeSchema\n(validation_error / cycle_detected / tool_not_allowed / forbidden / not_found /\nconflict / upstream_error / internal_error) so the Web Component branches on a\nstable code (clear cycle / allowlist / validation messages).\n\nCompile-time drift guards tie the create/structural editable fields to the SDK\nSkill type. 0.2.0 + CHANGELOG. +14 contract tests (31 total). All workspaces\ngreen (contract 31, bff 26, web 12). package-lock regenerated (also fixes the\npre-existing bff sdk 0.14->0.15 drift).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(258): keep Phase-1 route builders byte-for-byte unchanged (Codex)\n\nCodex review flagged that the Phase-1 getSkill/updateSkill builders had been\nmechanically rewritten to the new `enc` alias (runtime-identical to\nencodeURIComponent, but not byte-for-byte the Phase-1 source). Reverted both to\ninline encodeURIComponent; `enc` is used only by the new Phase-2 builders, so\nthe Phase-1 surface is now provably untouched. No behavior change.\n\n(Codex L1 — a reverse create→schema drift guard — is intentionally omitted: it\ncannot typecheck because Skill.sourceUrl is `string|null` while the create\nschema''s is `string|undefined`; the one-directional guard matches the existing\n_updateTracksSkill pattern.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJOCvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaLsQAFth1KmHPMaHjwTZKX/Llln2\n+mZa14ksVfUBCT5r6QE7E8lrsgm5cAjoFujBfzT9dCqVGdL5E0JUcZMsrrrdhiFJ\nl5qat+3h2AVneskQ6icdwpo+i63QLOguYjw5SQ3G2LRv+ldHFQF7O0SdoviWE71x\nCr5UdLJuaE4BscHLcrOGUNCSvlR/6YXtvUv3+ILMDZrPvnoYTmaxnrE4rbIhTYD2\nYSL5JqGjE6kFhJBpZlgk0/dpkC6AuHlo9bKikoj59dZ5cQwXiVfcktcI6MmZQA/P\nKLhM31lVI53eRfVaKjeaSgFzEp7Ye/bk5WAg2Iyvf6qMoLdk2hUZ7QcPaDe393uP\nziwxQgbVpv9YWU0eNwGIv3BUYOq2+1L3jFHEorKr4+IQCjWE4xV5eXn07BAdHiI1\n2sl3bqHI+Lby+ERFpmITrzGpUKEMxSxQ4v+Dp0UoMxWtNFcynGD3FQXzq+/VCymz\nw4OwvLAM3XQcSknYu