rs/calcifux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calcifux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calcifux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calcifux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calcifux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/calcifux","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/calcifux/tequio-core/commits/93277350fc6c44742d3acc22b71fc2d2b9c050fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T05:30:05Z","email":"17649380+calcifux@users.noreply.github.com","name":"calcifux"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T05:30:05Z","email":"17649380+calcifux@users.noreply.github.com","name":"calcifux"},"message":"feat: tequio.lazy + jornal scan — imports perezosos y análisis extensible (0.1.6)\n\ntequio.lazy: import perezoso opt-in (`from tequio.lazy import openpyxl`) para\nlibs pesadas que el auto-discovery cargaría en procesos que no las usan (el\nworker que no genera Excel, el cron efímero). Difiere hasta el primer uso.\n\njornal scan (tequio.scan): análisis extensible — modelo de la app (imports +\nestado eager/lazy, vía el discovery) + capacidades auto-descubiertas (@capability:\nlazy/http/db/mongo). Solo reporta. Kernel idéntico a milpa (drift-guard verde).","tree":{"sha":"e413193629f15bf6a512e0d529e041018c2e6f59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/calcifux/tequio-core/git/trees/e413193629f15bf6a512e0d529e041018c2e6f59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/calcifux/tequio-core/git/commits/93277350fc6c44742d3acc22b71fc2d2b9c050fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17649380?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calcifux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calcifux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github