jEyOTMyNw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tombell/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tombell/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tombell/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tombell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tombell/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tombell","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tombell/f1-dashboard/commits/40cbf252c6de3d4fc67be7a9805ffd335876d2e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T17:35:00Z","email":"tomb@tombell.dev","name":"Tom Bell"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T17:35:00Z","email":"tomb@tombell.dev","name":"Tom Bell"},"message":"Fix driver data fallback to scope by meeting_key instead of global\n\nThe driver enrichment fallback in LiveDashboard, MeetingDetail, and\nLiveDataSections was calling getDrivers() with no filter, returning\ndriver records across all years/meetings. This caused wrong team names,\ncolours, and driver data when viewing sessions from different years\n(e.g. a driver at Ferrari in 2024 showing as Williams from 2026 data).\n\n- getDrivers() now accepts optional meetingKey param\n- Fallback queries use getDrivers(undefined, meetingKey) to scope\n  driver lookups to the current meeting weekend\n- Cache is keyed by meeting_key so switching between years correctly\n  invalidates stale data\n- Removed unused ''void meetingKey'' placeholder in LiveDataSections","tree":{"sha":"633a465d930a26f85304dcb047fa7266c41a135c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tombell/f1-dashboard/git/trees/633a465d930a26f85304dcb047fa7266c41a135c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tombell/f1-dashboard/git/commits/40cbf252c6de3d4fc67be7a9805ffd335876d2e2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuse